  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 1,
  "properties": {
    "panels": [
      {
        "key": "intro-lesson-1-review-html-basics-61a318a8-0e6e-442e-920f-d0392510ea07",
        "text": "Remember how **HTML** is the core language that tells web browsers how to display information? It's the essential backbone for every webpage you see online.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/fdc3675b1330d16f065ec3c99734f97c-intro-lesson-1-review-html-basics-panel-1-b80306d5-20ca-49b8-8479-61563e18b590.png",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "intro-lesson-1-review-html-basics-cdc7e447-ab17-43f3-9f1a-fc70d9c2a4bb",
        "text": "We start with the `<!DOCTYPE html>` declaration, then wrap everything within the `<html>` tags. Inside, we have the hidden `<head>` and the visible `<body>`.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/39bc1d35a6896ba59d101f7745b7b67c-intro-lesson-1-review-html-basics-panel-2-83cfefad-7ead-4534-b5f9-45c48bba98d6.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "key": "intro-lesson-1-review-html-basics-3d85de1d-838a-4d41-90f1-24a7802b9e4b",
        "text": "Inside the `<body>`, we use special tags to structure content. An `<h1>` tag creates a main heading, and a `<p>` tag is used for paragraphs of text.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/18fcd38654b1e19d7555ad16f520d76c-intro-lesson-1-review-html-basics-panel-3-6b2f8352-b2fc-4424-9f8b-79435c481098.png",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "intro-lesson-1-review-html-basics-74f5522c-5908-40a8-93d1-eeadd19d571d",
        "text": "By combining these structural tags and content elements, you've learned to build a complete, simple webpage that browsers can understand and display to users!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/695eda1d94e62811ee924847d6c137ff-intro-lesson-1-review-html-basics-panel-4-2d690c68-7ced-48d9-8649-b2880946d031.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-left"
      }
    ],
    "generate_prompt": "Review the concepts learned: the importance of HTML, basic document structure, and how to use `<h1>` and `<p>` tags to add text. Summarize how these elements combine to form a simple web page."
  },
